{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":" whose out-neighbors come from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"text":"). It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches instead: Traversal’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ShortestPaths’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states over a finite set, number them and use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a grid is numbered row-major.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once each, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"type":"text","text":". Each target is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yields them by count, rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"lazy.filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a fixed neighbor list: the filter calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its predicate per element and keeps the unfiltered iterator’s state, and in the benchmarks on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1000 × 1000 grid it cost 1.2–1.8× the precomputed row (breadth-first layers, components,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"type":"text","text":", unique even among parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight closure reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a closure has no identity and is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L38"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/s9EscapableP":{"title":"Swift.Escapable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/OutEdges":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/outedges","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.OutEdges","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OutEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OutEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The positions of the edges leaving one vertex, in row order: ranks 0, 1, …, each with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"target, checked to be a vertex as it is read."}]},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/Successors":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Successors","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Successors","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ImplicitDirectedGr